---
version: 1.0
name: "Default 6-Step Dynamic Attributes"
dynID: "default-six-steps-001"
universeID: "Synex"
inheritsFrom: "universal-dynamics"
author: "System Designer"
tags: ["6-step", "baseline-0.5", "dynamic-attributes"]
abstract: "Provides baseline dynamic attributes for the six-step system, each step referencing a default synergy of 0.5."

dynamic_attributes:
  # Each key corresponds to one of the six steps,
  # with subfields referencing seeds, offsets, or synergy expansions.

  potential:
    baseline: 0.5
    fluctuation_range: "-0.2 to 0.2"
    offset_range: "-0.05 to 0.05"
    description: "Step 1: Seeds new expansions. Defaults to 0.5 for easy detection of offset."
  
  symmetry:
    baseline: 0.5
    fluctuation_range: "-0.15 to 0.15"
    offset_range: "-0.05 to 0.05"
    description: "Step 2: Ensures balanced constraints around 0.5."

  flow:
    baseline: 0.5
    fluctuation_range: "-0.3 to 0.3"
    offset_range: "-0.1 to 0.1"
    description: "Step 3: Governs expansions or velocity of iteration from 0.5."

  connectivity:
    baseline: 0.5
    fluctuation_range: "-0.25 to 0.25"
    offset_range: "-0.1 to 0.1"
    description: "Step 4: Merges expansions. Linking synergy states around a stable center (0.5)."
  
  emergence:
    baseline: 0.5
    fluctuation_range: "-0.4 to 0.4"
    offset_range: "-0.15 to 0.15"
    description: "Step 5: Realizes new synergy patterns while referencing midpoints at 0.5."
  
  recursion:
    baseline: 0.5
    fluctuation_range: "-0.1 to 0.1"
    offset_range: "-0.05 to 0.05"
    description: "Step 6: Feeds results back to seeds. Typically narrower range to keep cycic stability near 0.5."

principles:
  # Optionally reference the universal synergy or law files
  synergy_measure: "E_total"
  cycic_threshold: "epsilon_cyclic"
  notes: "Adjust fluctuation_range or offset_range as needed for each step."

seed: 0.5
use_unified_seed: true

description: |
  This .dyn file unifies default dynamic attributes for the six steps—Potential, Symmetry, Flow, Connectivity, Emergence, and Recursion.
  Each step starts at a baseline of 0.5, highlighting any offset from equilibrium.
  Integrate with synergy engine logic to maintain cycic harmony (E_total ≈ ε_cyclic).
...
